    "https://jobs.unwsp.edu/jobs/engagement-director-on-air-host-knws-iowa-united-states-582daddc-ad71-49bd-a7b8-34bf36dcf69c": {
      "title": "Engagement Director & On-Air Host, KNWS",
      "description": "Engagement Director & On-Air Host, KNWS - Iowa, United States Engagement Director & On-Air Host, KNWS - Iowa, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Engagement Director & On-Air Host, KNWS Iowa, United States, 50421 Staff FT Exempt Add to favorites View favorites Title: Engagement Director & On-Air Host, KNWS VP Area: VP - Media Department: KNWS - Waterloo Position Compensation: $52,632 - $58,480 / year Location: Waterloo, Iowa - KNWS Who We Are: Northwestern is a faith-driven community, UNWavering in our Christ-centered principles and identity as those who profess faith in Jesus. Rooted in the unshakable foundation of God’s Word and our calling to impact His world, our mission and vision flow from these core values, expressed through Christ-centered higher education at the University of Northwestern – St. Paul and through gospel outreach and faithfulness with Northwestern Media. Please Note: To avoid actual or perceived conflicts of interest, applications by candidates who have a relative employed within the same area of the organization may be subject to an eligibility review as part of the application process. Position Summary: The Engagement Director & On-Air Host at Life 101.9 serves as a key ambassador for the station, growing audience reach while strengthening relationships with listeners through compelling on-air content and community engagement. This role plans and executes outreach initiatives, promotions, digital and social media efforts, and live appearances, while supporting marketing, press, and audience database growth. Key Responsibilities: Engagement: • Provides strategic direction, in collaboration with station leadership, for community and listener engagement initiatives to ensure alignment with Life 101.9’s mission, brand, and growth goals. • Leads and oversees outreach events, concerts, contests, remotes, promotions, and other public-facing activities, equipping staff and volunteers to represent the station with excellence. • Develops and nurtures partnerships with vendors, community organizations, local businesses, churches, ministries, and media partners to expand Life 101.9’s visibility and influence. • Guides Life 101.9’s digital engagement, ensuring the website, app, and social media platforms present timely, relevant, and compelling content that supports programming and promotions. • Provides leadership to volunteer engagement, ensuring volunteers receive clear communication, positive experiences, and meaningful opportunities to support key initiatives. • Oversees promotional resources, managing the planning, ordering, and use of station merchandise to support events and brand consistency. • Collaborates cross-functionally to grow the listener database through intentional engagement at events and promotional activities. On-Air Host: • Hosts assigned on-air segments with preparation, personality, and alignment to format guidelines to strengthen listener connection. • Contributes additional content, including voice tracked shifts and digital/social elements, to support consistent programming across platforms. • Represents Life 101.9 at community events, maintaining a friendly, warm, and professional presence during appearances, evenings, and weekends as needed. • Perform other duties as requested or assigned. Because our community is a significant part of our mission and the development of our students and listeners, all employees serve as ministers of the gospel of Jesus Christ by actively partnering with the University to disciple students as they grow intellectually and spiritually, and with Northwestern Media to lead people to Christ and nurture believers to maturity in their faith. Qualifications: Required: • High school diploma or GED equivalent required • Minimum of one (1) year of previous experience in promotions or event planning • Maintain a growing, personal relationship with Jesus Christ, reflect His character in all interactions, and faithfully uphold and embrace Northwestern’s mission, Doctrinal Statement and Declaration of Christian Community Nice to Have: • Bachelor’s degree • Previous broadcast experience • Three (3) years of previous promotions/event planner experience Key Skills: • Independent & Teamwork: Capable of working both independently and collaboratively, with minimal supervision. • Confidentiality: Maintains discretion and handles sensitive information appropriately. • Organizational Skills: Strong time management and problem-solving abilities; able to prioritize and meet deadlines with attention to detail. • Technical Proficiency: Intermediate to advanced computer skills, including Microsoft Office and related software. • Written & Verbal Communication: Strong writing, editing, proofreading, and verbal communication skills. • Flexibility: Willingness to work occasional evenings and weekends as needed. • Travel: Willingness and ability to travel occasionally for work-related purposes. • Financial Oversight: Experience managing budgets and financial resources within assigned responsibilities. • Driver’s License: Valid driver's license. • Background Check: Must pass initial and ongoing background checks as a condition of employment. Work Environment: The work environment involves working for a suburban, Christian university or Christian owned and operated radio station alongside those with a demonstrated commitment and personal relationship with Jesus Christ, a commitment to the mission and values of Northwestern, and an agreement to abide by all Northwestern policies. All applicants must be authorized to work for any employer in the United States as we are unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment visa. Northwestern's Benefits Overview Apply Now First Name (required) bbdc5ddd Last Name (required) 2b72d161 Email (required) 27a5e874 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert f678d692 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can s